          "question": "e-153",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "The position of a race car along a straight track, measured in feet from the starting line, is given by the function $s(t),$ where $t$ is the time in seconds. The values of $s(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $s(t)$ | $0$ | $3$ | $7$ | $12$ | $19$ |\n\nApproximate the velocity $s'(t)$ at the time $t=0.1$ using a forward difference approximation.",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/example-153.json",
          "file_sha256": "32b9ea9dbb725470382967c4063fdc551fc53f3f0160ed3891a280fa199894db"
